Implementing a text editor with multiple lists (multitext) in Angular involves several steps. Below is a high-level guide to help you get started:

### 1. **Setup Your Project**
   - First, make sure you have Node.js and npm installed on your machine.
   - Create a new Angular project using `ng new` or by running `npx create-angular-cli@latest my-app --style=scss`.

### 2. **Install Required Packages**
   - For a basic text editor functionality, you might need:
     ```bash
     ng add @angular/material
     ```
   - For multitext support, you can use the `ngx-multitext` package which provides an easy way to handle multi-line inputs.

   Install `ngx-multitext` via npm:
   ```bash
   npm install ngx-multitext
   ```

### 3. **Create the Text Editor Component**

#### Step 3.1: Create the MultiTextComponent

```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { MultitextService } from 'ngx-multitext';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-multi-text',
  templateUrl: './multi-text.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./multi-text.component.css']
})
export class MultiTextComponent {
  constructor(private multitextService: MultitextService) {}

  // Example data for initial content
  data = [
    "Line 1",
    "Line 2\nThis is a new line.",
    "Line 3"
  ];

  // Method to update the text
  updateText(index: number, value: string): void {
    this.data[index] = value;
    this.multitextService.updateData(this.data);
  }
}
```

#### Step 3.2: Update the Template (`multi-text.component.html`)

```html
<div>
  <textarea [(ngModel)]="text" [data]="data"></textarea>

  <!-- Button to add new line -->
  <button (click)="addNewLine()">Add New Line</button>
</div>

<app-multiple-lists></app-multiple-lists>
```

#### Step 3.3: Implement the Multiple Lists Component

```typescript
import { Component, OnInit } from '@angular/core';
import { Observable } from 'rxjs';
import { map } from 'rxjs/operators';

// Assuming you have an observable list of items here
const itemList$: Observable<any[]> = /* ... */;

@Component({
  selector: 'app-multiple-lists',
  template: `
    <ul *ngFor="let item of itemList$ | async">
      <li>{{item}}</li>
    </ul>
  `,
  styles: []
})
export class MultipleListsComponent implements OnInit {
  itemList$: Observable<any[]>;

  ngOnInit(): void {
    // Initialize the observable if needed
    this.itemList$ = /* ... */;
  }

  addItem(item: any): void {
    this.itemList$.next([...this.itemList$, item]);
  }
}
```

### 4. **Update the Main App Component**

In your main app component, you'll want to connect these components together. Here's an example:

```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { MultiTextComponent } from './multi-text/multi-text.component';
import { MultipleListsComponent } from './multiple-lists/multiple-lists.component';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  standalone: true,
  imports: [MultiTextComponent, MultipleListsComponent],
  template: `
    <app-multi-text></app-multi-text>
    <app-multiple-lists></app-multiple-lists>
  `,
  styles: []
})
export class AppComponent {
  title = 'your-title-here

