To create a dynamic webpage that changes the appearance of the sun based on the time of day, we can use PHP to generate HTML content dynamically based on the current date and time. We can then use CSS to style the HTML elements accordingly.
Here's an example of how you might achieve this:
PHP Code:
```php
<?php
$now = new DateTime();
$currentDay = $now->format('l');
?>
```
This will set up some basic variables in your PHP script. `$now` is a `DateTime` object representing the current date and time, and `$currentDay` stores the name of the current day (e.g., "Monday").
CSS Code:
```css
.sun {
  width: 100px;
  height: 100px;
  background-color: #FFFFCC; /* Bright yellow */
}
.red-orange-swirl {
  transform-origin: center;
  animation-name: sunSwirl;
  animation-duration: 3s;
  animation-iteration-count: infinite;
}
@keyframes sunSwirl {
  from {transform: rotate(0deg);}
  to {transform: rotate(360deg);}
}
```
The first part of the CSS code sets up two classes - `.sun` for the sun element itself, and `.red-orange-swirl` for the swirling effect. The `.sun` class has some basic styling properties like size and color. The `.red-orange-swirl` class uses CSS animations to create a rotating sun shape with red and orange colors near the edges.
HTML Code:
```html
<div id="sun" class="<?php if ($currentDay == 'Sunday') echo 'red-orange-swirl'; ?>">
  <img src="http://www.example.com/sun.jpg" alt="Sun">
</div>
```
In the above HTML code, we're creating a `<div>` element with an ID of "sun". This div will contain our sun image. The class attribute contains either the default value (`'sun'`) or the additional class we defined earlier (`'red-orange-swirl'`). Based on the current day being Sunday, we'll add the `red-orange-swirl` class to the sun div.
Finally, we have a simple `<img>` tag inside the sun div, which should display your custom sun image. The `alt` attribute provides alternative text for screen readers.
Remember to replace `http://www.example.com/sun.jpg` with the actual URL pointing to your sun image file. Also, adjust the dimensions and styles as per your requirements. This is just a basic example to give you an idea about implementing such functionality. Depending on your specific needs, you may need to make further adjustments.

