To display an image with a caption under it on a web page using HTML and CSS, you need to ensure that the image is properly centered and styled as required. Here's how you can achieve this:

### HTML Code

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Image with Caption</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      background-color: #f4f4f4;
      color: #333;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 20px;
    }

    .container {
      width: 80%;
      margin: 0 auto;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .img-container {
      position: relative;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .img-container img {
      max-width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      border-radius: 5px;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
    }

    .caption {
      position: absolute;
      bottom: -20px; /* Adjust the offset if needed */
      left: 0;
      right: 0;
      background-color: white;
      padding: 10px;
      opacity: 0;
      transition: opacity 0.3s ease-in-out;
    }

    .img-container:hover .caption {
      opacity: 1;
    }

    .caption h1 {
      margin-top: 0;
      font-size: 18px;
      font-weight: bold;
      color: #333;
    }

    .caption p {
      margin-bottom: 10px;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: #666;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="container">
  <div class="img-container">
    <a href="https://www.example.com" target="_blank"><img src="image.jpg" alt="Image" /></a>
    <div class="caption">
      <h1>Caption goes here</h1>
      <p>Description or additional information about the image.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:

1. **Container Div**: The `container` div is used to center the image and add some padding around it.

2. **Image Container (`.img-container`)**:
   - The `position: relative;` ensures the child elements (`img`, `.caption`) are positioned absolutely within the container.
   - The image is set to `max-width: 100%;` and `height: auto;` to maintain aspect ratio and scale appropriately.
   - A `box-shadow` effect is applied for visual appeal.
   - The `.caption` is made `absolute` and positioned at the bottom of the container so it overlays the image.
   - When hovering over the image, the caption becomes visible by increasing its `opacity`.

3. **Hover Effect**: On hover, the opacity of the caption increases to reveal its contents.

This structure ensures your image has a clean, centered layout with a descriptive caption below it. Adjustments may be necessary based on specific design requirements or additional styling needs.

