To blend different audio files and create a realistic experience of a summer day using Java programming language, you can use the Java Sound API (javax.sound) which provides access to sound devices such as microphones, speakers, and MIDI instruments.
Here's an example code snippet that plays two audio files sequentially:
```
AudioInputStream audioIn1 = AudioSystem.getAudioInputStream(new File("path/to/audio/file1.mp3"));
AudioInputStream audioIn2 = AudioSystem.getAudioInputStream(new File("path/to/audio/file2.mp3"));
Clip clip1 = AudioSystem.getClip();
clip1.open(audioIn1);
Clip clip2 = AudioSystem.getClip();
clip2.open(audioIn2);
try {
    clip1.start();
    Thread.sleep(5000); // wait for 5 seconds before starting clip2
    clip2.start();
} catch (Exception e) {
    e.printStackTrace();
}
```
To add artificial sounds to enhance the overall experience, you can use plugins or libraries that generate synthetic audio data. Some popular options include JASRACO, Synthesis Toolkit, and LADSPA.
For creating a well-defined structure for the audio narrative, you can use a combination of loops, conditional statements, and event-driven programming techniques. For example, you could have a loop that continuously plays the background sounds while waiting for user input to start specific events (e.g., pressing "p" to play music). You could also use conditionals to control the playback speed and volume based on the current scene being played.
As for visualizing the audio file and its components, you can use various tools and software packages such as Audacity, VLC Media Player, or Adobe Audition. These programs allow you to analyze the waveform, spectrum, and other properties of the audio file, and also to manipulate the audio using graphical interfaces.
Regarding LaTeX code for visualization, it depends on what kind of visualization you want to create. There are many LaTeX packages available for audio processing and analysis, such as `audio` package, `wavesurfer.js`, and `ffmpeg`. However, these packages require additional setup and configuration to work properly.

